/ The review of an app of your own (CustomAppsController#review): what it will be able to do, in
/ words, the warning, and the owner's password to add it (or save the changes). The app file goes
/ back in a hidden field, its image pinned, with its logo (_logo_fields); the root helper checks it
/ all again when it's saved.
- app = @app
- editing = @editing
- repo_tag, digest = app.image_parts
- errors = app.errors

/ Back sends the file back to the form (CustomAppsController#review with back), as it was described:
/ a form of its own, as a form's token is for its own address (per-form CSRF tokens)
= form_tag custom_apps_review_path, id: 'custom-app-back' do
  input type="hidden" name="back" value="1"
  input type="hidden" name="source" value="file"
  input type="hidden" name="editing" value=editing
  input type="hidden" name="manifest" value=app.text
  = render 'logo_fields'
p.kai-apps-back
  button.btn.btn-link.p-0.kai-custom-back type="submit" form="custom-app-back"
    = lucide_icon('chevron-left', size: 16)
    | Back to describing it

.kai-custom
  .kai-custom-review-head
    = render 'apps/app_logo', name: app.name, logo: logo_src
    .kai-app-pills
      span.kai-pill.kai-pill-amber Custom
      - if app.data['category'].present?
        span.kai-pill.kai-pill-outline = app.data['category'].to_s.capitalize

  - if errors[:file]
    p.kai-notice.kai-notice-alert#custom-app-problem role="alert" = "That doesn't work yet: #{errors[:file]}"

  section.kai-app-panel aria-labelledby="custom-can-head"
    h2#custom-can-head What it will be able to do
    dl.kai-app-facts.kai-custom-facts#custom-facts
      - app.facts.each do |label, words|
        dt = label
        dd
          - if label == 'Image'
            code = repo_tag
            br
            span.kai-custom-hint = "This exact build (sha256:#{digest}), until you change it"
          - else
            = words
      - if app.data['sign_in'].present?
        dt Sign in
        dd = app.data['sign_in']

  section.kai-custom-warning aria-labelledby="custom-warn-head"
    = lucide_icon('alert-triangle', size: 24)
    div
      h2#custom-warn-head It isn't from the Amahi-kai catalog
      p
        | Nobody has checked this image for you. It runs boxed in like the catalog's apps, but a bad image
          could still misuse what you give it: its folders, the shares you choose, and the internet. Add
          apps only from people you trust.

  section.kai-app-panel aria-labelledby="custom-confirm-head"
    h2#custom-confirm-head = editing ? 'Save the changes' : 'Add it'
    = form_tag (editing ? custom_apps_save_path(editing) : custom_apps_create_path), id: 'custom-app-confirm' do
      input type="hidden" name="id" value=app.id
      input type="hidden" name="manifest" value=app.text
      = render 'logo_fields'
      .kai-custom-field.kai-custom-narrow
        label.form-label for="custom-password" = editing ? 'Your password, to change an app of your own' : 'Your password, to add an app of your own'
        input.form-control#custom-password type="password" name="password" autocomplete="current-password" required=true aria-describedby=("custom-password-problem" if errors[:password])
        - if errors[:password]
          p.kai-custom-problem#custom-password-problem role="alert" = errors[:password]
      p.kai-custom-hint
        | Asked even though you're signed in, so a page left open, or a stolen sign-in, can't add an app.
        - if editing
          |  Saving then updates it: its data is copied first, and it goes back if it doesn't come up. A
            change only to how it's listed doesn't restart it.
        - else
          |  Install then asks which shares to give it, if any, and opens the install window.
      .kai-custom-actions
        button.btn.btn-outline-secondary type="submit" form="custom-app-back" Back
        button.btn.btn-primary type="submit" data-disable-with="Saving…" = editing ? 'Save and update' : 'Add it'
